 that it also  potentially provides  a new target in the treatment of  reducing the severity of senescence  for example if the degradation of cert  one could be inhibited  it may delay senescent onset and then  this may  synergize with sat1 activators such as  resveratrol  because in at least one of the figures  in this paper resveratrol wasn't able to  prevent the degradation of cert one  however other studies show  that it can activate set one activity  and so by preventing degradation and  activating the activity of that one  you can see how it could have a  combinatorial impact  but this actually raises another  question why would a senescent cell want  to get rid of cert one  and so i'm going to speculate a little  which is something i don't tend to do  too much on this channel because i like  to base my opinions on facts  but anyway during senescence there are  lots of changes that occur within the  nucleus  and a lot of that's due to the chromatin  rearranging  and cert one decelerates histones  proteins which are really  important in this process and also it's  dc's latest p53 if i forgot to mention  that earlier  and so by degrading sart1 and removing  it from the nucleus  it may help in this reorganization of  chromatin within the nucleus  to establish senescence which is  interesting and cool and i guess  would be interesting to follow up in  further research  and more on from that it'd be very  important to try and work out  what other proteins besides that one and  lamin b1  that seem to get targeted by this  autophagy  mediated degradation especially if ways  of inhibiting this process  is going to be sought after because it'd  be good to examine if there's going to  be any  negative consequences and also just  whilst i was making this video i was  thinking about how  the cert 1 regulation could be impacting  on the circadian rhythm because i  mentioned in a previous video how cert  one activity was necessary for  increasing one of the components  female 1 and its binding on dna and  yeah this pretty much is kind of opening  pandora's box i don't really know how  the circadian rhythm gets impacted in  semesters  and so yeah i think that's in the whole  area in itself  that was worth investigation but that  one is obviously important in this  process  and what was important in lots of  processes so if you can take anything  away from this video you should take  away that  anyway as we've come to the end i hope  you have learned something on this video  and as always thanks for listening

